Err... you mean like... telnetToTiles ?   I believe the patched server 
version works approximately like you describe.  One caveat, is that an 
approach like that exposes more information about the items being viewed 
than the current approach.  If a person cooks up their own client, they 
can determine *by examining the glyph* whether or not that green gem is 
a worthless piece of glass or an emerald.  The telnetToTiles client I 
wrote doesn't do this, but I saw the possibility when I was writing it. 
  In a tourney, that would be unfair advantage.

Client and patch found at: http://www.geocities.com/jdhilts@sbcglobal.net/

